Allow non-French phone numbers when registering a Person.

PersonForm.vue's vue-tel-input binds :onlyCountries="['FR']", which
hardcodes the country-code dropdown to France only. validCharactersOnly
plus the library's own validation then reject any number typed for a
different country (e.g. +47 / 0047 for Norway), regardless of what the
user types in the text box.

Confirmed on the rendered form (GitHub issue #6): the dropdown shows only
France (+33) and manually entering another country code does not work.

Fix: drop the onlyCountries restriction so the dropdown offers every
country vue-tel-input knows about. defaultCountry="FR" is left in place
so the field still defaults sensibly for the common case.

--- a/opensilex-front/front/src/components/persons/PersonForm.vue
+++ b/opensilex-front/front/src/components/persons/PersonForm.vue
@@ -87,7 +87,6 @@
         <vue-tel-input
             v-model="phone_number"
             defaultCountry="FR"
-            :onlyCountries="['FR']"
             validCharactersOnly
             @validate="validatePhone"
             @input="updatePhoneNumber"
